<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # You Can Save Water By... – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Environment and Recycling</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> You Can Save Water By...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write a short report on a class activity. Interactive: Edit classmates' narratives for clarity and coherence.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a short report about a class recycling activity, describing how practices have changed over time (e.g., "Before, people didn't recycle as much, but now we separate items for recycling.")<br>Can edit for clarity a peer's story about recycling (e.g., "Add more details about the report on the class activity.")<br>Can compose a short description of actions to help the environment (e.g., "We should recycle paper and plastic.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 20px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e0e0; color: #1a5276; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e0e0; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0e0e0; color: #1a5276; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of a clean river and a polluted river, then asks students to brainstorm and write down short phrases or single words describing what they see and how they feel. Students are then asked to complete the sentence stem "Before, people did ____, but now we should ____." individually in their notebooks for 2 minutes. This activates prior knowledge about past vs. present practices and the modal 'should'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to write a simple sentence contrasting past and present actions, for example, by writing on the board: "In the past, people wasted water, but today we save it. We should turn off the tap." The teacher clearly articulates the sentence, emphasizing the "-ed" endings in "wasted" and the contrast between 'waste' and 'save'. The teacher also demonstrates how to form an advice sentence with 'should'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'wasted,' did it happen yesterday or today?" (Expected answer: "Yesterday.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What word helps us give advice about protecting the planet?" (Expected answer: "'Should'.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short narrative excerpt (100-120 words) describing a hypothetical school recycling campaign and its impact, presented as a mini-report. It explicitly uses past simple vs. present practices, first conditional, and modal 'should' related to vocabulary like 'recycle', 'waste', 'environment', 'clean', 'save'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students understand simple descriptions of events and activities related to environmental actions, distinguishing between past and present situations. They recognize advice given using modal verbs.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main topic of this text?" (Expected answer: "A school recycling activity.") "What changed over time?" (Expected answer: "How students recycle/care for the environment.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read the report and decide if statements like "In the past, students recycled plastic" (False) or "If we recycle, we protect the planet" (True) are correct.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match sentences from the report to their purpose: (e.g., "This sentence describes a past action," "This sentence gives advice," "This sentence shows a cause-effect.").</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using past simple vs. present practices, first conditional, and modal 'should'. They integrate vocabulary: recycle, waste, environment, planet, save, protect, carefully, often, important. Practice pronunciation of '-ed' endings in verbs like 'saved' /d/, 'wanted' /ɪd/, 'watched' /t/ as they write and silently rehearse sentences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides sentences with blanks and a word bank (e.g., *recycled, waste, should, protects, saved, environment*). Students complete sentences like: "Before, people often ____ water, but now we try to ____ it." or "We ____ collect plastic if we want to ____ the planet."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Expansion/Combination):</b> Students are given simple statements and asked to expand them into two sentences, contrasting past/present or adding advice. E.g., "Kids threw trash." (Student writes: "Before, kids threw trash. Now, they carefully recycle. We should reduce waste.") Or "We use too much energy." (Student writes: "If we use too much energy, we will harm the environment. We should save energy.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Sentence Writing & Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students write 3-4 sentences each about different ways to save water, focusing on using 'should' and at least one 'if...then' sentence. They then exchange their sentences with their partner and check for correct use of 'should' and 'if' clauses, as well as target vocabulary. They can also briefly practice pronouncing their written sentences, focusing on the stress contrasts and '-ed' endings.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual writing task followed by peer editing. Students will write a short report (60-80 words) describing a hypothetical class recycling activity and how practices have changed over time regarding water or waste, then edit a classmate's report.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students imagine their class organized a "Water Saving Week" or "Recycling Drive" in their school or community. They are to write a short report for a school newsletter.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The report must include:
                            <ul>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A description of what people did "before" (using past simple, e.g., "In the past, we often wasted water," or "people didn't recycle plastic often").</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A description of current practices or what the class did during the activity (using present practices, e.g., "Now, we turn off the tap carefully," or "we recycle paper and plastic").</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one piece of advice using "should" (e.g., "We should always save energy.") or a cause-effect statement using the first conditional (e.g., "If we save water, we will protect our planet.").</li>
                                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Target vocabulary (e.g., recycle, waste, environment, planet, save, clean, important).</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After writing, students exchange reports with a partner. Each student reads their partner's report and provides constructive feedback (Sociolinguistic: Collaborate in problem-solving) using two sentences: one positive comment and one suggestion for improvement for clarity or coherence (e.g., "Add more details about the report on the class activity," "Check the verb tense here.").</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment of learning)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during peer editing and review of selected student reports for specific linguistic features.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their written report and the peer feedback they received/gave. The teacher quickly scans the reports for completion of criteria.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher):</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of past simple vs. present practices (e.g., "Before, we wasted..." vs. "Now we save...")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of 'should' for advice.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of at least one first conditional sentence (cause-effect).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (recycle, waste, environment, planet, save, protect).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence of the report.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Quality of peer feedback (constructive criticism).</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students write short answers to the following questions:
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing I learned about writing a report on environmental actions?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was it easy or difficult to give advice to my classmate? Why?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Review, self-assessment, and future planning)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing about past and present environmental actions did I find most challenging, and why?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I use 'If...then' sentences more effectively when talking about the environment?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., Peer editing encouraged deeper engagement, students effectively used 'should'.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Provide more sentence starters for the first conditional, dedicate more time to pre-writing brainstorming for struggling writers.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How did the pronunciation practice (stress, -ed endings) support writing accuracy? (e.g., Helped students internalize tense changes, which translated to more accurate written forms).</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Mediation & Integration), students will consolidate their understanding of environmental issues by summarizing information and collaborating on a 21st Century Skills Project, potentially presenting their reports or creating a campaign poster based on their written advice.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>